>HEAD

  DATAID="SP1"
  ACQBY="AusMT test fixture"
  PROSPECT="Single period fixture"
  LOC="Fixture"
  LAT=-37.316700
  LONG=143.000000
  EMPTY=1.0E+32

>INFO   MAXLINES=1000

  MINTED FIXTURE - NOT CUSTODIAN DATA. The shape it carries was measured on
  the seventy-eight NFREQ=1 files in the AusMT GDS staging at
  GDS/_staging/surveys - reference shape
  southeast-australia-1971/transfer_functions/edi/Ararat.edi - which are
  themselves AusMT-minted digitisations of published array tables where one
  period is all the source printed. A single-period EDI is well formed. The
  reader is not: its descending-frequency assertion indexes the second
  frequency unconditionally. No byte is copied from a staged file: the
  identity is invented and the values are minted for this test.

>=DEFINEMEAS

  MAXCHAN=3
  MAXRUN=999
  MAXMEAS=99999
  UNITS=M
  REFTYPE=CART
  REFLAT=-37.316700
  REFLONG=143.000000

 >HMEAS ID= 1001.001 CHTYPE=HX X =  .000000  Y =  .000000  AZM=   0.0000
 >HMEAS ID= 1002.001 CHTYPE=HY X =  .000000  Y =  .000000  AZM=  90.0000
 >HMEAS ID= 1003.001 CHTYPE=HZ X =  .000000  Y =  .000000  AZM=  .000000

>=MTSECT
  SECTID=SP1
  NFREQ=    1
  HX = 1001.001
  HY = 1002.001
  HZ = 1003.001

 >!****FREQUENCIES****!
 >FREQ NFREQ=   1  ORDER=DEC //    1
    0.20833E-03
 >!****TIPPER PARAMETERS****!
 >TXR.EXP ROT=0.0 //    1
    0.55000E+00
 >TXI.EXP ROT=0.0 //    1
    0.14000E+00
 >TXVAR.EXP ROT=0.0 //    1
    0.90000E-01
 >TYR.EXP ROT=0.0 //    1
   -0.12000E+00
 >TYI.EXP ROT=0.0 //    1
    0.90000E-01
 >TYVAR.EXP ROT=0.0 //    1
    0.90000E-01

>END
